From 31d212ec1794fc46554aee42bfc4c499ad078d4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergei Iudin <tsipa740@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Nov 2021 16:45:24 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [PATCH] Dummy patch to bump hotfix version

klp-build refuses to emit a module when a hotfix changes no object on
this architecture, and the build then ships an empty placeholder RPM.
Add a no-op to a cold function so every KLP contains one changed
function and a real module is produced everywhere.

version_proc_show() is only reached by reading /proc/version, so the
livepatch transition never has to wait for it to leave a task's stack,
and the inserted instruction is unreachable in practice.

asm volatile() rather than barrier(): a compiler barrier changes no
machine code here, because the seq_printf() call already clobbers
memory, so klp-build would still see an unchanged function.
---
 fs/proc/version.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/fs/proc/version.c b/fs/proc/version.c
--- a/fs/proc/version.c
+++ b/fs/proc/version.c
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 
 static int version_proc_show(struct seq_file *m, void *v)
 {
+	asm volatile("nop");	/* KLP: no-op, forces a changed function */
 	seq_printf(m, linux_proc_banner,
 		utsname()->sysname,
 		utsname()->release,
--
